{
  "count": 98,
  "cues": [
    {
      "sentence_id": "P01-01",
      "start": 1.8,
      "end": 3.516,
      "text": "Don't open the box."
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": "P01-02",
      "start": 3.816,
      "end": 8.676666666666668,
      "text": "Pandora's box is one of the best-known\nimages from Greek myth."
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": "P01-03",
      "start": 8.976666666666667,
      "end": 12.825686274509804,
      "text": "A woman is given a box, she\nis told never to open it,"
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": "P01-03",
      "start": 12.825686274509804,
      "end": 16.526666666666667,
      "text": "and when she does, every\nevil in the world escapes."
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": "P01-04",
      "start": 16.826666666666668,
      "end": 20.248,
      "text": "But in the oldest source\nwe have, there is no box."
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": "P01-05",
      "start": 20.548000000000002,
      "end": 24.688625000000002,
      "text": "And the story it tells is stranger\nthan the one we remember."
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": "P02-01",
      "start": 28.766666666666666,
      "end": 34.29765258215962,
      "text": "In this episode, we follow Pandora\nfrom a Greek poet of around 700 BCE,"
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": "P02-01",
      "start": 34.29765258215962,
      "end": 40.0656807511737,
      "text": "through ancient storage jars and a later\nfable, to a Renaissance scholar's"
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": "P02-01",
      "start": 40.0656807511737,
      "end": 45.596666666666664,
      "text": "book of proverbs and the paintings\nthat gave her the box we know today."
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": "P03-01",
      "start": 51.0,
      "end": 53.82523255813954,
      "text": "The earliest account comes from Hesiod,"
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": "P03-01",
      "start": 53.82523255813954,
      "end": 57.230000000000004,
      "text": "the same poet who described\nthe birth of Medusa."
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": "P03-02",
      "start": 57.53,
      "end": 60.9977509469697,
      "text": "In two of his poems,\nthe Theogony and the Works"
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": "P03-02",
      "start": 60.9977509469697,
      "end": 64.16395833333334,
      "text": "and Days, Pandora's\nstory begins with fire."
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": "P03-03",
      "start": 64.46395833333334,
      "end": 69.102625,
      "text": "Prometheus has stolen fire\nfrom Zeus and given it to humans."
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": "P03-04",
      "start": 69.402625,
      "end": 72.09258333333334,
      "text": "Zeus answers with a gift of his own."
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": "P04-01",
      "start": 73.0,
      "end": 78.72795833333333,
      "text": "At his command, the smith god Hephaestus\nshapes a young woman from earth and water."
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": "P04-02",
      "start": 79.02795833333333,
      "end": 82.00525,
      "text": "Athena teaches her weaving\nand dresses her."
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": "P04-03",
      "start": 82.30525,
      "end": 85.579875,
      "text": "Aphrodite gives her grace,\nand painful longing."
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": "P04-04",
      "start": 85.879875,
      "end": 92.28054166666666,
      "text": "And Hermes gives her, in Hesiod's words,\na shameless mind and a deceitful nature."
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": "P04-05",
      "start": 92.58054166666666,
      "end": 96.03504741379311,
      "text": "Because all who lived\non Olympus gave her a gift,"
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": "P04-05",
      "start": 96.03504741379311,
      "end": 98.84183333333334,
      "text": "she is named Pandora, the \"all-gifted.\""
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": "P05-01",
      "start": 103.6,
      "end": 106.41666666666666,
      "text": "In the Theogony, she is not even named."
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": "P05-02",
      "start": 106.71666666666665,
      "end": 111.37046204620461,
      "text": "Hesiod calls her a beautiful\nevil, a trap set for humankind,"
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": "P05-02",
      "start": 111.37046204620461,
      "end": 114.68333333333332,
      "text": "and presents her as the first\nof all women."
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": "P05-03",
      "start": 114.98333333333332,
      "end": 117.87529166666666,
      "text": "His poems are openly hostile to women."
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": "P05-04",
      "start": 118.17529166666667,
      "end": 120.99722456140351,
      "text": "That view belongs to Hesiod and his time,"
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": "P05-04",
      "start": 120.99722456140351,
      "end": 124.71391666666666,
      "text": "and it is one more reason\nto read the source carefully."
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": "P06-01",
      "start": 127.4,
      "end": 131.068625,
      "text": "In the Works and Days, Hesiod\ntells what happened next."
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": "P06-02",
      "start": 131.368625,
      "end": 133.9423355263158,
      "text": "Prometheus had warned his brother"
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": "P06-02",
      "start": 133.9423355263158,
      "end": 137.29595833333335,
      "text": "Epimetheus never to accept\na gift from Zeus."
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": "P06-03",
      "start": 137.59595833333333,
      "end": 139.84791666666666,
      "text": "But Epimetheus accepted her."
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": "P06-04",
      "start": 140.14791666666667,
      "end": 145.68991666666668,
      "text": "Before this, people had lived free from\nevils, from hard work, and from sickness."
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": "P06-05",
      "start": 145.98991666666666,
      "end": 150.55325,
      "text": "Then she lifted the great lid of a jar\nand scattered what was inside."
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": "P06-06",
      "start": 150.85325,
      "end": 153.78925,
      "text": "Countless troubles spread among humankind."
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": "P07-01",
      "start": 157.66666666666666,
      "end": 164.84129166666665,
      "text": "The Greek word Hesiod uses is pithos, a\nlarge storage jar for grain, oil, or wine."
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": "P07-02",
      "start": 165.14129166666666,
      "end": 169.2585548245614,
      "text": "This one, made on Crete\naround 675 BCE and now"
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": "P07-02",
      "start": 169.2585548245614,
      "end": 173.83329166666667,
      "text": "in the Louvre, is about\none and a half meters tall."
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": "P07-03",
      "start": 174.13329166666665,
      "end": 177.30124999999998,
      "text": "Hesiod does not say\nwhere the jar came from."
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": "P07-04",
      "start": 177.60125,
      "end": 180.39304408914728,
      "text": "And the only warning in his poem is about"
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": "P07-04",
      "start": 180.39304408914728,
      "end": 183.4572083333333,
      "text": "accepting the gift, not\nabout opening the jar."
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": "P08-01",
      "start": 186.1,
      "end": 188.30929166666667,
      "text": "Only one thing stayed inside."
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": "P08-02",
      "start": 188.60929166666665,
      "end": 191.34191666666666,
      "text": "Hope remained beneath the rim of the jar."
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": "P08-03",
      "start": 191.64191666666667,
      "end": 195.80991666666665,
      "text": "Before it could fly out, the lid\nstopped it, by the will of Zeus."
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": "P09-01",
      "start": 197.06666666666666,
      "end": 198.46666666666667,
      "text": "Why hope?"
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": "P09-02",
      "start": 198.52729166666666,
      "end": 201.84729166666665,
      "text": "Readers have argued about\nthis line for centuries."
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": "P09-03",
      "start": 202.14729166666666,
      "end": 205.52729166666666,
      "text": "Is hope kept safe for us,\nor kept away from us?"
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": "P09-04",
      "start": 205.82729166666667,
      "end": 211.61925,
      "text": "The Greek word, elpis, can mean hope,\nbut also expectation of what is to come."
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": "P09-05",
      "start": 211.91925,
      "end": 214.011875,
      "text": "Hesiod does not explain."
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": "P10-01",
      "start": 219.5,
      "end": 223.648,
      "text": "Greek artists also told\nthe story of Pandora's making."
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": "P10-02",
      "start": 223.948,
      "end": 229.19552525252524,
      "text": "The ancient traveler Pausanias wrote\nthat her birth was shown in relief"
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": "P10-02",
      "start": 229.19552525252524,
      "end": 233.84333333333333,
      "text": "on the base of the great statue\nof Athena inside the Parthenon."
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": "P10-03",
      "start": 234.14333333333335,
      "end": 236.34133333333332,
      "text": "The statue itself is lost."
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": "P10-04",
      "start": 236.64133333333334,
      "end": 239.5968156862745,
      "text": "But this small copy from Roman times still"
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": "P10-04",
      "start": 239.5968156862745,
      "end": 242.62266666666667,
      "text": "carries a version\nof that scene on its base."
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": "P11-01",
      "start": 244.06666666666666,
      "end": 246.88195833333333,
      "text": "And the jar did not always hold evils."
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": "P11-02",
      "start": 247.18195833333334,
      "end": 251.12098397435898,
      "text": "A later Greek fable, collected\nunder the name of Babrius,"
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": "P11-02",
      "start": 251.12098397435898,
      "end": 254.49729166666665,
      "text": "tells of a jar that Zeus\nfilled with good things."
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": "P11-03",
      "start": 254.79729166666667,
      "end": 257.606625,
      "text": "A man who could not resist lifted the lid,"
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": "P11-03",
      "start": 257.606625,
      "end": 260.4159583333333,
      "text": "and the good things\nflew up to the heavens."
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": "P11-04",
      "start": 260.71595833333333,
      "end": 262.892625,
      "text": "Only hope was left behind."
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": "P11-05",
      "start": 263.192625,
      "end": 266.38191666666665,
      "text": "In this fable, Pandora is not even named."
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": "P12-01",
      "start": 268.2,
      "end": 270.15595833333333,
      "text": "So where did the box come from?"
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": "P12-02",
      "start": 270.45595833333334,
      "end": 274.60075983146066,
      "text": "The change is usually\ntraced to the early 1500s,"
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": "P12-02",
      "start": 274.60075983146066,
      "end": 278.304625,
      "text": "more than two thousand years after Hesiod."
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": "P12-03",
      "start": 278.604625,
      "end": 282.4486856060606,
      "text": "The Dutch scholar Erasmus\nretold the story in Latin,"
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": "P12-03",
      "start": 282.4486856060606,
      "end": 286.066625,
      "text": "in his famous collection\nof proverbs, the Adages."
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": "P12-04",
      "start": 286.366625,
      "end": 291.95861904761904,
      "text": "In this edition, printed\nin Venice in 1508, where Hesiod"
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": "P12-04",
      "start": 291.95861904761904,
      "end": 297.75395833333334,
      "text": "had pithos, a great jar, Erasmus\nwrote pyxis, a small box."
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": "P12-05",
      "start": 298.0539583333333,
      "end": 303.2932916666667,
      "text": "And in his retelling, it is Epimetheus,\nnot Pandora, who opens it."
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": "P13-01",
      "start": 304.2,
      "end": 305.59999999999997,
      "text": "Why a box?"
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": "P13-02",
      "start": 305.86133333333333,
      "end": 309.19006666666667,
      "text": "Scholars have suggested\nthat Erasmus may have been"
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": "P13-02",
      "start": 309.19006666666667,
      "end": 312.6546666666666,
      "text": "thinking of another story,\nthe Roman tale of Psyche."
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": "P13-03",
      "start": 312.95466666666664,
      "end": 315.863448275862,
      "text": "She is sent to the underworld\nto bring back"
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": "P13-03",
      "start": 315.863448275862,
      "end": 318.97999999999996,
      "text": "a small box, and is warned\nnot to look inside."
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": "P13-04",
      "start": 319.28,
      "end": 321.56929166666663,
      "text": "On the way back, she opens it."
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": "P13-05",
      "start": 321.86929166666664,
      "end": 324.34325,
      "text": "Whatever the reason, the word stuck."
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": "P14-01",
      "start": 328.76666666666665,
      "end": 331.64733333333334,
      "text": "Erasmus's book was read across Europe."
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": "P14-02",
      "start": 331.9473333333333,
      "end": 338.5545833333333,
      "text": "Later artists gave Pandora many kinds of\ncontainers: caskets, chests, and vessels."
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": "P14-03",
      "start": 338.8545833333333,
      "end": 344.35525,
      "text": "Some still showed a great jar,\nlike this print from the 1500s."
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": "P14-04",
      "start": 344.65524999999997,
      "end": 348.2040574534161,
      "text": "But over time, the box\nbecame the familiar image,"
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": "P14-04",
      "start": 348.2040574534161,
      "end": 352.34433281573496,
      "text": "and \"Pandora's box\" became\nan everyday phrase in English,"
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": "P14-04",
      "start": 352.34433281573496,
      "end": 356.55854166666666,
      "text": "for something that brings many\ntroubles once it is opened."
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": "P15-01",
      "start": 358.3666666666667,
      "end": 361.032625,
      "text": "So was Pandora's box ever a box?"
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": "P15-02",
      "start": 361.332625,
      "end": 364.56458333333336,
      "text": "In Hesiod, it is a great storage jar."
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": "P15-03",
      "start": 364.8645833333333,
      "end": 368.1379166666667,
      "text": "In a later fable, the jar\nholds good things."
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": "P15-04",
      "start": 368.4379166666667,
      "end": 372.7325416666667,
      "text": "In a Renaissance book of proverbs,\nit becomes a small box."
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": "P15-05",
      "start": 373.0325416666667,
      "end": 376.8405,
      "text": "And in paintings, it\nis whatever the artist imagined."
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": "P16-01",
      "start": 378.93333333333334,
      "end": 382.646,
      "text": "The box we know is not\nthe oldest part of the story."
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": "P16-02",
      "start": 382.946,
      "end": 384.846625,
      "text": "It is one of the newest."
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": "P16-03",
      "start": 385.14662500000003,
      "end": 387.4739166666667,
      "text": "Every story has an origin."
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": "P16-04",
      "start": 387.77391666666665,
      "end": 390.74858333333333,
      "text": "Sometimes, even the objects in it do."
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": "P17-01",
      "start": 393.56666666666666,
      "end": 398.396,
      "text": "This video is based on ancient\ntexts and public museum collections."
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": "P17-02",
      "start": 398.69599999999997,
      "end": 401.65257142857143,
      "text": "The narration uses synthetic speech,"
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": "P17-02",
      "start": 401.65257142857143,
      "end": 405.5946666666667,
      "text": "and some images are\nAI-generated reconstructions."
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": "P17-03",
      "start": 405.89466666666664,
      "end": 409.840625,
      "text": "Sources and terms of use are\nlisted in the description."
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": "P17-04",
      "start": 410.140625,
      "end": 412.909498015873,
      "text": "If you enjoyed this story, please like"
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": "P17-04",
      "start": 412.909498015873,
      "end": 416.26129166666664,
      "text": "the video and subscribe\nfor more quiet origins."
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": "P17-05",
      "start": 416.56129166666665,
      "end": 418.33391666666665,
      "text": "Thank you for watching."
    }
  ],
  "timing": "Exact synthesized sentence boundaries; within-sentence pages weighted by text length",
  "script_matches_ignoring_layout_whitespace": true
}
